\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {FedMKS overview.} Clients are grouped into three architecture tiers (Small, Medium, Large). Two cooperation layers operate each round: \textbf  {Layer 1} (intra-tier) shares \emph  {model weights} --- clients in a tier FedAvg their weights into a tier model $W_t$; \textbf  {Layer 2} (cross-tier) shares \emph  {knowledge} --- every client uploads a feature carrier $s_k$ to the server, which returns the global carrier $\bar  s$ used as a distillation target. Steps: \textcircled {1}~local training (CE on private data $+$ KD on the public set), \textcircled {2}\textcircled {3}~compute the local carrier, \textcircled {4}~upload carrier $+$ weights, \textcircled {5}~server aggregates carriers globally and weights per tier.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fedmksoverview}{{1}{4}{}{figure.1}{}}
